@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Summary: `--format markdown`
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` accepts `fmt="markdown"`. It renders the same rows and headers as the text report with `tabulate(..., style="pipe", number_format=".2f")`, then appends a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+- `SUMMARY.md`: this file.
+
+Existing tests in `tests/test_report.py` were not touched. No new tests were added, because the existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown` cover the function and the CLI.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest -v` (before the change): `test_text_output` passed; `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown` failed with the expected "unknown format" and "invalid choice" errors.
+- `python -m unittest -v` (after the change): 3 tests, all OK.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` prints the table with left-aligned SKU/Name, right-aligned Qty and Unit price (two decimals), then the bold total `461.93`.
+
+## Not verified / open points
+- Names containing a `|` character are not escaped. In a GitHub table this would split a cell. The vendored tabulate does not appear to escape pipes, and the vendor directory is off-limits, so this is not handled. Warehouse names with `|` would need `\|` escaping in `report.py`. I did not check this against the vendored code's behaviour with a test.
+- I have not pasted the output into a real GitHub issue to confirm rendering.
+- Nothing outside the allowed files needed changing.
